Stores every individual debit or credit line of a journal entry (account.move), forming the atomic level of the General Ledger.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Detailed lines of invoices, bills, payments, bank statements, and manual entries
General Ledger postings and trial balance
Account reconciliation (residual amount tracking)
Analytic accounting & cost/profit center allocation
Tax computation and tax report lines
Financial reporting, aged balances, and P&L breakdowns

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
move_id → account.move (required, parent)
account_id → account.account (required)
debit, credit, balance, amount_currency
partner_id, date, name (label)
reconciled (boolean), full_reconcile_id, matched_debit_ids / matched_credit_ids
analytic_account_id, analytic_tag_ids
tax_ids, tax_line_id, tax_tag_ids
product_id, quantity, price_unit
Computed: price_subtotal, currency_id, company_currency_id

Critical Hooks: _compute_balance, reconcile, remove_move_reconcile, onchange_account_id, tax & analytic engines
Security: Strict record rules linked to parent move + account manager rights

RAG Routing Keywords:
journal item, move line, account move line, general ledger line, gl line, debit credit line, journal entry line, reconciled line, unreconciled item, analytic line, tax line, ledger entry, posting line
Related Models (most joined):

account.move (parent)
account.account
res.partner
account.full.reconcile & account.partial.reconcile
account.analytic.account
account.tax
account.bank.statement.line

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
account.move.line is the most granular Odoo accounting model holding every debit/credit line with account_id, debit, credit, partner_id, analytic dimensions, tax details, and reconciliation status. It forms the backbone of the General Ledger, drives all financial reports, reconciliation engine, analytic accounting, and is created automatically from invoices, payments, bank statements, and manual journal entries.